Task: Add property_fy_facts (migration 054) (Phase 2, Tier 1)
Track: fy_tax_pack_20260729

SUMMARY
New table public.property_fy_facts, PK (property_id, financial_year_end).
Columns: ownership_pct (numeric(5,2) default 100, 0 < pct <= 100),
days_available_for_rent, private_use_days (both 0..366 for leap years),
notes, created_at, updated_at.

FILES
- supabase/migrations/054_property_fy_facts.sql (new)
- lib/supabase/database.types.ts - PropertyFyFacts row type hand-added
  plus the Tables entry, per the hand-maintained-types rule in CLAUDE.md

WHY PER-YEAR
Ownership share and rental availability change over time. Storing them on
properties would mean today's value silently rewrites history: a property
sold down from 100% to 50% would restate last year's figures at the new
share and overstate the deduction. Each year is its own row.

financial_year_end is the calendar year the FY ends in (2026 for 2025-26),
matching lib/tax/fy.ts.

RLS follows migration 030: read via has_property_read_access (owner,
active co-owner, or property viewer), write via has_property_write_access
(owner or co-owner only). An accountant holding a viewer share stays
read-only.

